imgui
------------------------------------------
Dear ImGui is a bloat-free graphical user interface library for C++. It outputs
optimized vertex buffers that you can render anytime in your 3D-pipeline
enabled application. It is fast, portable, renderer agnostic and self-contained
(no external dependencies).

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libGL1-23.3.6-1
  libSDL2_2.0_0-2.32.74-1
  liballegro5.2-5.2.11.3-1bl4
  libfreetype6-2.13.3-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libglfw3-3.5.1-1bl1
  libglut3-3.4.0-1
  libimgui-devel-1.93.0-1bl1
  libimgui1-1.93.0-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libGL-devel-23.3.6-1
  libSDL2-devel-2.32.74-1
  liballegro-devel-5.2.11.3-1bl4
  libfreetype-devel-2.13.3-1
  libglfw-devel-3.5.1-1bl1
  libglut-devel-3.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/ocornut/imgui

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/archive/v1.93.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack imgui-1.93.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./imgui-1.93.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/imgui-1.93.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/imgui-1.93.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libimgui1-1.93.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libimgui-devel-1.93.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

